1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,600
I lost 30, 30 members of my family in two days.

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,420
Half of my family is gone.

3
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:11,380
Every time I talk to my mom, she tries to tell me her final goodbye.

4
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,440
She tells me, I miss you.

5
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,880
I really want to be able to hug you again.

6
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:18,600
And I tell her, Mama, why are you not strong?

7
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:20,160
Come on, you're going to hug me again.

8
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:23,020
And I close the line and I cry for two hours.

9
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:26,080
I cry at how unjust this world is.

10
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:28,740
I cry at how the world does not see my humanity.

11
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:31,360
I cry at how silent the world is.

12
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:34,640
Not only silent, but complicit in war crimes and massacres

13
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:36,600
that are being committed against me and my people.

14
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:38,420
No one is safe in Gaza.

15
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:41,180
I don't know if my family is going to make it or my friends.

16
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:42,460
I don't know who's next.

17
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:43,600
I don't know.

18
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:44,700
And I don't want to know.

19
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:46,340
I just wanted to stop.

20
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:48,480
I just want to wake up from this nightmare.

21
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:53,560
Everything started on Saturday where I lost my best friend.

22
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:56,760
The friend that I would call whenever I needed to cry

23
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:58,700
or whenever I needed to share good news.

24
00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:02,640
Ibrahim and I covered the 2022 aggression on Gaza.

25
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:06,040
He was the person who would shoot my videos and I was the reporter.

26
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:09,200
His dream was to become a world-renowned photographer.

27
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:12,480
In the morning, he texted the group chat of our friends and he said,

28
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:14,140
the situation is escalating.

29
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:15,000
I'm going to the office.

30
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:17,060
So I texted him privately and I said,

31
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:18,780
Ibrahim, please take care.

32
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:22,300
My messages didn't go through to Ibrahim and I kept trying to reach him,

33
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:23,020
but I couldn't.

34
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:25,980
My colleague said that Ibrahim is missing.

35
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:36,300
And it's been 10 days and I feel like I just lost him like two minutes ago.

36
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:40,860
Like, I still don't believe it's real.

37
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:42,880
I genuinely don't believe it.

38
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:47,440
I just feel like I'm in a long nightmare and I'm not waking up, you know.

39
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:52,600
He told me in the 2022 aggression, he told me,

40
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:54,680
Yara, you're going to be the next Shirin Abu Aqli.

41
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:57,640
They killed her, but you are Shirin Abu Aqli.

42
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:59,860
Please don't ever give up journalism.

43
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:03,480
And he told me, we'll report every aggression side by side.

44
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:10,980
And I genuinely thought we would, you know, but I didn't know that Israel would just kill him,

45
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:16,000
just like they did with Shirin Abu Aqli, just like they did with Yasir Murtaja.

46
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:21,020
Ibrahim became a journalist in the first place because he was so inspired by Yasir's Murtaja

47
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:23,660
and he wanted to carry on his message.

48
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:27,820
And I don't know, I never imagined that I'd lose Ibrahim.

49
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:28,840
He was so young.

50
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,440
He was only 21 years old.

51
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:32,260
He was only 21 years old.

52
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:37,340
I wish you can give me more time to talk about every single member of my family

53
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:40,860
who was killed in detail and tell you about their dreams, their ambitions,

54
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:43,620
what they wanted to be and what they've done in life.

55
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:46,520
I want to tell you about my eldest uncle.

56
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,200
He had dementia.

57
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:51,760
He barely remembered anything about his life, but he was always smiling.

58
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:54,400
He was telling me that he loved me every time he saw me.

59
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:56,180
I want to tell you about the children.

60
00:02:56,620 --> 00:02:59,640
In my uncle's house only, eight children have been murdered.

61
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:02,180
Those children, I have so many memories.

62
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:04,840
I remember them calling me and telling me,

63
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:06,560
Yara, can you please come for a sleepover?

64
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:08,600
Yara, we want to do something with you.

65
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:12,740
I used to love babysitting children, so I used to babysit them whenever I went home.

66
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:16,940
My cousin, who was murdered yesterday, she was a bride.

67
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,160
She was supposed to get married next month.

68
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,040
She literally prepared everything.

69
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:22,900
She even picked her wedding dress.

70
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:31,300
She's been so excited for her wedding and she's been doing it for months and months and everything's gone just like that.

71
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:35,740
My cousin and her children, her four children, they were Swedish nationals.

72
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:40,460
They were visiting Gaza and then, you know, they got trapped and they couldn't leave.

73
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:42,060
They're Swedish nationals.

74
00:03:42,620 --> 00:03:42,740
Yeah.

75
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:45,360
And they were killed.

76
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:46,960
How are these terrorists?

77
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:50,020
How is my family that I grew up with my whole life?

78
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:51,440
People who taught me how to love.

79
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:53,300
People who taught me how to live.

80
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:54,720
And there's so many.

81
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:57,100
I even feel guilty talking about my family.

82
00:03:57,220 --> 00:04:00,980
I'm not the more than 3,000 Palestinians who have been killed in the last 10 days.

83
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:05,280
I feel guilty because every single one of the 3,000 was not a number.

84
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:08,380
Every single one of the 3,000 had the story.

85
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:09,760
They were journalists.

86
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:10,740
They were doctors.

87
00:04:10,940 --> 00:04:11,740
They were teachers.

88
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:12,760
They were dreamers.

89
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:14,760
They were so much.

90
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:16,920
They were humans after all.

91
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:17,800
They were humans.

92
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,300
They had dreams and ambitions.

93
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:22,960
I don't even have time to grieve my family.

94
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:26,400
I don't have time to cry or talk about them.

95
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:29,460
I have to report and I have to work and I have to educate the West.

96
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:33,620
And I have to tell them why they shouldn't be asking me if I should condemn Hamas or not.

97
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:37,100
But they should be asking me about Israel and about what Israel is doing.

98
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:40,760
They shouldn't ask me and dehumanize me when I'm a Palestinian journalist,

99
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:43,760
not a spokesperson of any political party.

100
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:48,500
They should ask me about the 30 members of my family who are not militants,

101
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:51,080
not a group, not part of any group.

102
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:52,960
They should be asking me these questions.

103
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:58,640
I just want everyone to know this is not an Israel-Hamas war as Israel portrays it to be.

104
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:01,220
Let's imagine a world where Hamas does not exist.

105
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,120
Imagine the West Bank.

106
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:04,940
You know, Hamas is not in control there.

107
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:06,680
What has been happening in the West Bank?

108
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:07,700
There's apartheid.

109
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:10,480
There is military detention of minors.

110
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:11,620
There is torture.

111
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:14,460
There is killing of Palestinians every single day.

112
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:15,560
There is oppression.

113
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:17,440
There is complete home demolition.

114
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:20,400
Everything you can imagine they're doing in the West Bank.

115
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:23,240
So, why are you asking me about Hamas now?

116
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:26,520
Why are you not asking me about how I didn't see my dad for six years?

117
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:30,940
And then I went, I saw him, I saw him only for a few months and then he was, he died.

118
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,080
He got really sick and died.

119
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,460
I couldn't see him for six years.

120
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,840
They prevented me from being with my father.

121
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:38,220
They prevented me from having a normal childhood.

122
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:42,980
I had to be in therapy for years and years to get over the sound of bombs,

123
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:46,240
the pictures of murdered children in front of my eyes

124
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:48,880
and the guilt that I felt that I survived and they didn't.

125
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:51,340
Why are you not asking me about the thousand Palestinian children

126
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:52,840
that have been killed in the last 10 days?

127
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:56,260
Why are you not asking me about how my best friend, a journalist,

128
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,340
marked clearly as press was killed?

129
00:05:58,440 --> 00:05:59,560
Why are you not asking me this?

130
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:01,260
I'm not a spokesperson for Hamas.

131
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:03,200
I'm not a part of any political party.

132
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:03,960
I'm a journalist.

133
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,720
My job is to report on what's happening.

134
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:08,960
My colleague, Mu'taz Azayzeh, they bombed his house,

135
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:11,340
killing so many of his family members.

136
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:14,540
My other colleague, Ali Jadallah, just in the last 10 days,

137
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:17,520
they've killed his brother, an elderly father.

138
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:22,920
My boss and mentor, Rushdie Sarraj, was killed as he was in his home on an airstrike.

139
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:26,760
It was literally targeted the assassination of him because he was a journalist.

140
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:30,200
They're literally targeting journalists and trying to threaten them.

141
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:33,080
If you are doing your job, we will kill you.

142
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:35,900
And this is what Israel has been doing for the last decades

143
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:40,480
because journalists are the only way for the world to know what's actually happening in Palestine.

144
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:45,080
I don't remember a day in my life where there was peace.

145
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:49,540
I was only 8 years old when I witnessed the first aggression on Gaza.

146
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:51,100
It was in 2008.

147
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:53,400
And then it was in 2012.

148
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:55,160
And then it was in 2014.

149
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:59,340
And only in 2014 that I was able to comprehend what's happening.

150
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:02,900
Like when I was 8 and I was 12, I didn't really understand death.

151
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,720
I didn't understand white phosphorus or chemical weapons.

152
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:06,740
I was a child.

153
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:10,360
The only thing I wanted to do is play and be around my family.

154
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:14,540
When I was 14, I was in the hospital crying, telling my parents,

155
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:16,120
I don't believe you're alive.

156
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:22,140
I was so in shock and in PTSD, post-traumatic distress disorder,

157
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:25,700
that I genuinely believed my family were completely killed

158
00:07:25,700 --> 00:07:29,020
because of the amount of killings I've seen as a 14-year-old.

159
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:32,860
If you're a Palestinian living in Gaza and you were born in 2000,

160
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:36,420
you would have been living through six aggressions by now.

161
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:40,340
This is not just the first time that Israel decides to completely wipe out

162
00:07:40,340 --> 00:07:43,260
complete neighbourhoods and attack civilians and attack hospitals.

163
00:07:43,740 --> 00:07:46,120
But this is the most barbaric attack that we've seen.

164
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:49,120
Palestinians in Gaza have not seen one day of peace.

165
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:52,960
Not one day that my family and I felt safe in our homes.

166
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:55,380
What is it like to be a Palestinian?

167
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,600
What is it like to grow up in Gaza?

168
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:59,540
I don't have one answer.

169
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,500
I have millions of answers.

170
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:04,940
Growing up in Gaza meant that by the age of 14,

171
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:09,880
I saw literally body parts of people, children being murdered in front of my eyes.

172
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:15,500
I remember I used to say, if I survive this aggression, if I make it alive,

173
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:19,200
I'm going to write a book and tell the whole world about what's happening.

174
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:20,820
And I was only 14 years old.

175
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:23,140
I didn't realise what was happening to me then.

176
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:25,100
This is what it's like to grow up in Gaza.

177
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:29,540
But it's also all the nights that I spent talking to my dad about politics

178
00:08:29,540 --> 00:08:32,520
and how Palestine will be free one day

179
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:34,360
and how my culture is important

180
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:37,620
and how I should be committed and steadfast on my land

181
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:40,840
and how my mum cooks Palestinian food for us

182
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:43,200
and teaches us the recipes that my grandma made

183
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:45,320
and that her great-grandma made

184
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:47,520
and that her great-great-grandma made.

185
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:50,400
Being Palestinian is so painful

186
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:53,900
but at the same time, I would never want to be anything but Palestinian

187
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:58,840
because I know my people, they're the strongest people I've ever met.

188
00:08:59,260 --> 00:09:00,780
They endure so much.

189
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:03,820
Being Palestinian means that you have friends in the West Bank

190
00:09:03,820 --> 00:09:05,700
but you're unable to meet them or see them.

191
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,500
Being Palestinian means that you're a Muslim or Christian

192
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:11,940
and want to go pray in Al-Aqsa Mosque or in the Church of Nativity

193
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:14,600
and you can't just simply because you're from Gaza.

194
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:19,620
Being Palestinian means that your existence is threatened every single day

195
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:20,840
and not only that

196
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:23,420
but that every single day you need to wake up

197
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:25,420
and convince the world why you're a human

198
00:09:25,420 --> 00:09:28,720
and why your life matters just like the rest of the world.

199
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:30,260
Being Palestinian is hard.

200
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:31,940
Being Palestinian is difficult

201
00:09:31,940 --> 00:09:35,640
but being Palestinian is something I will never stop being.

202
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:38,360
For the first time in my life,

203
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:40,180
I feel like my voice is being heard

204
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:43,360
because I'm using my platform, I'm trying to work 24-7

205
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:44,780
to tell the world what's happening.

206
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:49,420
And even if news media organizations don't care about Palestinian voices

